! ---------------------------------------------------------------------
! CTS bootstrap - runs on each SDA fabric device that participates in
! TrustSec (classification, propagation, or enforcement).
!
! Prerequisites (pushed by CC's standard provisioning, not here):
!   - radius server dnac-radius_<ise_ip>                 (from network_settings.aaa_servers)
!   - aaa group server radius dnac-client-radius-group   (CC creates from same config)
!   - aaa server radius dynamic-author / client <ise_ip> (CC creates for CoA)
!
! What this template adds:
!   1. Parallel RADIUS path (ISE-CTS server + CTS-RADIUS-GROUP) sourced
!      from Gi0/0 in Mgmt-vrf. Required in this lab because CC's
!      standard provisioning pushes 'ip radius source-interface
!      Loopback0' in the global VRF - Loopback0 (RLOC) has no underlay
!      route to ISE in this topology. Production SDA fabrics that reach
!      ISE via the underlay can omit these blocks. The netascode catc
!      schema does not expose source-interface/vrf knobs in
!      network_settings.aaa_servers as of this version (verified against
!      catc/schemas/schema.yaml lines 362-381), so a dayn_template is
!      the SaC-supported escape hatch.
!
!      CC-managed 'dnac-*' RADIUS config is intentionally untouched so
!      the CC pipeline does not drift it on subsequent applies.
!
!   2. AAA method list 'CTS-AUTHZ-LIST' bound to CTS-RADIUS-GROUP
!      (replaces the previous 'group radius' binding, which inherited
!      the broken global 'ip radius source-interface Loopback0').
!
!   3. cts authorization list CTS-AUTHZ-LIST
!
!   4. dynamic-author CoA listener with Mgmt-vrf so ISE matrix updates
!      (RADIUS CoA, see ise/data/network_resources.nac.yaml
!      send_configuration_to_device_using: ENABLE_USING_COA) actually
!      reach the device. CC-pushed 'client 198.18.133.30 server-key'
!      without vrf is left alone - harmless, never matches inbound CoA.
!
!   5. cts credentials id/password per-device, wired through the
!      'device_name' and 'cts_password' Jinja variables declared in
!      catc/data/templates.nac.yaml and supplied per-device in
!      catc/data/multidomain_devices.nac.yaml. Stored in NVRAM keystore
!      (not running-config) so CC drift-detection ignores it; redeploy
!      with same values is a no-op. Earlier template comments warned
!      against pushing this from a template - that turned out to be
!      overcautious; the command accepts pre-CTS-init and is idempotent.
!
! COUPLING WARNING: ISE IP (198.18.133.30) and shared secret
! (C1sco12345) below are HARDCODED for the LTRXAR-3100 lab. They MUST
! stay in sync with:
!   - catc/data/network_settings.nac.yaml  aaa_servers.primary_ip / shared_secret
!   - ise/data/network_resources.nac.yaml  network_devices[*].radius.shared_secret
!                                          network_devices[*].trust_sec.device_password
! Change here = change in all three places. The per-device cts_password
! variable (in multidomain_devices.nac.yaml) MUST equal the ISE NAD
! trust_sec.device_password for that device.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------------

radius server ISE-CTS
 address ipv4 198.18.133.30 auth-port 1812 acct-port 1813
 key C1sco12345
!
aaa group server radius CTS-RADIUS-GROUP
 server name ISE-CTS
 ip vrf forwarding Mgmt-vrf
 ip radius source-interface GigabitEthernet0/0
!
aaa authorization network CTS-AUTHZ-LIST group CTS-RADIUS-GROUP
cts authorization list CTS-AUTHZ-LIST
!
aaa server radius dynamic-author
 client 198.18.133.30 vrf Mgmt-vrf server-key C1sco12345
!
cts credentials id {{ device_name }} password {{ cts_password }}
